<p>
<dt><b> 10 March 1997:</b>
<ul>
 <font size=-1>
 <li> Due to increased CPU usage, attacked the performance of plist.cgi (This
      is the binary that extracts and prints content listings). Implemented
      a new database index called <i>titles.xbt</i>. This allows looking up the complete
      contents in a single index entry instead of searching the entire database. This
      sped up the performance of plist.cgi by 270%. On the downside, it
      <b>greatly</i> increases the compile time of the database (by about 30%), and 
      requires another 600k of diskspace. The runtime performance increase should be 
      quite noticable.
 <li> Implemented a strange sorting algorithm for exact_author.cgi and a_exact_author.cgi
      which uses a combination of hash tables and linked lists. This sped up the 
      performance of the summary bibliographies by 175%. This should be noticable on 
      longer summary bibliographies.
 <li> Both of the above performance changes are fairly radical, involving much
      new code. Please report any problems you see.
 </font>
</ul>
<p>
